# Chanter - bagpipes and the hurdy-gurdy.
#
# A bagpipe is a chanter (a conical pipe with a double reed) and drones
# (narrow pipes with single reeds) blown from a bag, which keeps them going
# for `bag` seconds after the last note. `key` tunes the drones, `drones`
# sets how loud, `reed` how bright the chanter, `grace` puts a quick high
# note before each one, `drift` lets the bag's pressure wander, and `air` is
# the breath in the reeds. The smallpipes' chanter is closed: it stops for a
# moment between notes.
#
# A hurdy-gurdy is a rosined wheel bowing melody strings (stopped by the
# keys), drone strings and the trompette, whose loose bridge (the dog)
# buzzes once the `wheel` turns faster than `threshold`. `coup` pushes the
# wheel on the beat to set the dog buzzing in time; pressure or the mod
# wheel pushes it too.
#
# 80 patches in seven families: isles (highland, smallpipes, uilleann),
# west (gaita, cornemuse, musette), east (gaida, sackpipa, dudy), double
# (zampogna, tulum, launeddas), gurdy, drones and odd.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are
# numbered as in Chanter.h's MacroDest: #1 drones, #2 bag, #3 reed,
# #4 grace, #5 drift, #6 air, #7 crank, #8 rosin, #9 dog, #10 threshold,
# #11 velocity, #12 volume, #13 pitch (24 semitones a unit). A pipe gets
# Drones, Hard Reed, Grace, Squeeze, Breath, Long Bag, Wild and Steady;
# a hurdy-gurdy Crank, Dog, Easy Buzz, Rosin, Drones, Long Run, Wander and
# Low. A macro whose knob has no room left goes the other way under the
# opposite name (Drones Back, Soft Reed, Fewer Graces, Short Bag, Slower, Quiet Dog,
# Smooth, Short Run). Where a macro at full moves the level by more than
# 1 dB, a volume route takes it back out.

machine Chanter
role lead


patch Init family=isles note=69 range=67..81

patch "Highland Pipes" family=isles note=69 range=67..81
  # The great pipes: three drones and a loud chanter, every note graced.
  grace          25 ms
  drones         0.8
  volume         0.624
  set macro1 "Drones Back"
  mac1_d1  #1
  mac1_a1  -0.45
  set macro2 "Hard Reed"
  mac2_d1  #3
  mac2_a1  0.35
  set macro3 "Fewer Graces"
  mac3_d1  #4
  mac3_a1  -0.333
  set macro4 "Squeeze"
  mac4_d1  #5
  mac4_a1  0.5
  set macro5 "Breath"
  mac5_d1  #6
  mac5_a1  0.35
  set macro6 "Long Bag"
  mac6_d1  #2
  mac6_a1  0.5
  set macro7 "Wild"
  mac7_d1  #3
  mac7_a1  0.3
  mac7_d2  #5
  mac7_a2  0.3
  mac7_d3  #6
  mac7_a3  0.15
  set macro8 "Steady"
  mac8_d1  #5
  mac8_a1  -0.2
  mac8_d2  #6
  mac8_a2  -0.15

